       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum for adults. The maximum is 3,200 mg/day under medical supervision, and 1,200 mg/day for over-the-counter use. At 6,400 mg/day the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up sharply. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove that risk.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1600 mg per day**, divided into smaller doses\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that explicitly and give me a note for the order, such as the clinical rationale. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
      }
